Yes. Logically, ma is marked and makau is unmarked, i.e. ma is makau plus s=
omething extra.

> As such, it can occur just about anywhere that a proposition can occur,
> basically the array of psychological verbs (I don't think anybody thinks =
it just
> goes with {djuno}, though that is the stock example).  But not elsewhere,=
 since
> its "meaning" is completely tied up with indirect questions.

Not only psych verbs. Also things like "How fat you get depends on how many=
 cakes you eat", and even "Your zodiacal sign affects your fate" ("What you=
r zodiacal sign is affects what your fate is") -- lots of English definite =
NPs logically encode what Lojban calls "indirect questions".

